From 54e4a8d2b44cec22cc6ef0e88ae9f2fd9f31a26d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Keith Packard <keithp@keithp.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 22:35:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/18] test-posix: Check the signal characters

In a child that makes a pseudo-terminal its controlling terminal: INTR,
QUIT and SUSP send their signals to the whole foreground process group
and no other, are discarded, flush input unless NOFLSH is set, and are
data when disabled or without ISIG.
---
